        "theme":  "Philosophy",
        "summary":  "Thore Graepel, a core AlphaGo team member, argues that large language models lack genuine reasoning capabilities, contrasting their pattern-completion architecture with AlphaGo\u0027s explicit search mechanisms that evaluated future consequences. True reasoning, he contends, requires an inspectable epistemic state, separation of knowledge from its manipulation, and auditable decision-making — none of which current LLMs provide. The piece cautions against conflating LLM fluency with the cognitive capacity of reasoning.",
