        "summary":  "Will Douglas Heaven examines the paradox of public AI sentiment: majorities express nervousness and expect negative personal impact from AI, yet ChatGPT has reached one billion monthly users and over half of US adults now use chatbots. The author argues public distrust targets the companies driving AI adoption rather than the technology itself. Emerging regulatory frameworks and open-source alternatives are identified as potential forces for greater consumer agency.",
